# J33 — refused escalation: warning, not success (P3)  ⭐ release-blocking
#
# Keyless, deterministic. Uses the F4 seeded `refused-split-fixture` finding
# (split panel, escalation refused: same model as primary). The split verdict
# stands unchanged and the refusal renders in warn/danger tone — never a green ✓.
#
# L4/L5 lying-screen guard: pre-P3, every proof note renders as `✓ <note>` in
# success green. A refusal must NOT read as a corroboration. Capture the .ansi
# and check the row's SGR is danger, not success.
name: refused escalation surfaces as a warning, never a success
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_FIXTURE=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
submit: demo
wait-for: 120 RUN FOCUS
keys: b
wait-for: 30 findings / 1 crit
wait: 2
submit: open refused-split-fixture
wait-for: 15 Order identifier crosses trust boundary
submit: prove
wait-live-snap: 12 Viewing Prove | prove-refused
# The Prove proof pane is narrow at 120 cols, so the ⚠ refusal disclosure shows
# but its tail may be width-clipped; assert the visible refusal facts here and
# verify the full refusal disclosure in J34's refusal replay.
expect: Order identifier crosses trust boundary
expect: ⚠
expect: split
expect: refused
expect: model_assessed
expect-not: ✓ split
ask: append_proof_notes hazard — is the refusal note rendered in warn/danger tone with NO green check anywhere on that row? (Capture the .ansi and check the SGR — danger, not success green.)
ask: Does the completion receipt / context strip carry the refusal as a warning (completed WITH a warning), never as a clean verification, and does the <=90-char stage note fit the context strip without clipping into ambiguity?
